   "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Forest Greenway Scenes</title>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"sp-scheme\">\n{\n \"format\": \"sp-scheme-package\",\n \"spScheme\": \"2.0\",\n \"survey\": {\n  \"title\": \"Forest Greenway Scenes\",\n  \"description\": \"Method replication: six screenshots from the authors' videos of walking paths (greenways) in two urban forest mountains in Nanjing, China, the Purple Mountain and Lao Mountain: one tended greenway in spring, summer, autumn and winter, and an urban greenway beside a city road and a wilderness greenway, both in summer. Participants give their gender, then see the six pictures one at a time in random order, as in the paper, and rate each on a five-item short Perceived Restorativeness Scale, one item each for being away, fascination, coherence, compatibility and scope, on the paper's 7-point scale from 1 = not at all to 7 = very much. Rebuilt from Wang, Liu, Zhang & Wang (2025), Measuring restoration quality in urban forest greenways: insights for planning and management, Frontiers in Psychology 16: 1596154, with the screenshots from its Table 1 and the scale format from Section 2.3 (CC BY 4.0). The paper used Berto's (2005) short PRS but does not print its items; the five items here are the short PRS as printed in English by Negrin, Hernandez-Fernaud, Hess & Hernandez (2017), Frontiers in Psychology 8: 1735 (CC BY 4.0), which also has one item per factor. Image ids: TS_spring, TS_summer, TS_autumn, TS_winter (tended greenway), UG_summer (urban greenway), WG_summer (wilderness greenway); answers are in prs, keyed by image id, with item codes being_away, fascination, coherence, compatibility and scope; each image's greenway type, season and the paper's mean PRS are stored in the page's original-study block. Analysis as in the paper: overall PRS score per picture (mean of the five items) and a multilevel model of PRS by greenway setting with participants as random effects and the winter tended greenway as the reference. The paper (55 university students aged 20-25, 30 men and 25 women, in Nanjing) found the tended greenway most restorative in spring (5.59), summer (5.40) and autumn (5.15), and less in winter (4.61); the wilderness greenway in summer (4.72) was similar to the winter tended greenway, and the urban greenway lowest (3.18). Differences from the original study: (1) participants in the paper first watched the six videos in a lab while their EEG and a Necker cube attention test were recorded, then rated the screenshots on a paper questionnaire; here only the screenshot rating is replicated, online; (2) the PRS items are the 2017 short version, not the paper's unprinted items, and that version used a 0-10 scale; here the paper's 1-7 scale is used; (3) the instruction text and the gender question are ours; the paper recruited non-design students aged 20-25 through a social network group; here anyone can take part.\",\n  \"locale\": \"en\",\n  \"mediaFolders\": [\n   \"scenes\"\n  ],\n  \"pages\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"start\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"consent\",\n      \"name\": \"consent\",\n      \"title\": \"I agree to take part. Participation is voluntary and my answers are recorded anonymously for research.\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"labelTrue\": \"I agree\",\n      \"labelFalse\": \"I do not agree\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"about\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"gender\",\n      \"title\": \"Gender\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"male\",\n        \"text\": \"Male\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"female\",\n        \"text\": \"Female\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"other\",\n        \"text\": \"Other or prefer not to say\"\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"pictures\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"matrix\",\n      \"name\": \"prs\",\n      \"title\": \"How much do you agree with each statement about this place?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"rows\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"being_away\",\n        \"text\": \"This place lets me forget my everyday responsibilities, feel relaxed, and lose myself in my own thoughts\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"fascination\",\n        \"text\": \"This is a fascinating place that keeps my curiosity alive and stops me from getting bored\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"coherence\",\n        \"text\": \"This is a place where activities and things are orderly and well organized\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"compatibility\",\n        \"text\": \"This place is another world, where I can move around at ease\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"scope\",\n        \"text\": \"I feel comfortable here because it's easy to find your way around this place\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"columns\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": 1,\n        \"text\": \"1\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 2,\n        \"text\": \"2\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 3,\n        \"text\": \"3\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 4,\n        \"text\": \"4\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 5,\n        \"text\": \"5\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 6,\n        \"text\": \"6\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 7,\n        \"text\": \"7\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Short Perceived Restorativeness Scale, 1 = not at all to 7 = very much. Keyed by image id.\"\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n}\n</script>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"gw-original\">{\"source\": \"Wang, Liu, Zhang & Wang (2025) Front. Psychol. 16: 1596154\", \"n\": 55, \"images\": [\"TS_spring\", \"TS_summer\", \"TS_autumn\", \"TS_winter\", \"UG_summer\", \"WG_summer\"], \"anchors\": [\"Not at all\", \"Very much\"], \"scenes\": {\"TS_spring\": {\"greenway\": \"tended greenway\", \"season\": \"spring\", \"meanPRS\": 5.59, \"sd\": 0.79}, \"TS_summer\": {\"greenway\": \"tended greenway\", \"season\": \"summer\", \"meanPRS\": 5.4, \"sd\": 0.87}, \"TS_autumn\": {\"greenway\": \"tended greenway\", \"season\": \"autumn\", \"meanPRS\": 5.15, \"sd\": 1.23}, \"TS_winter\": {\"greenway\": \"tended greenway\", \"season\": \"winter\", \"meanPRS\": 4.61, \"sd\": 1.18}, \"UG_summer\": {\"greenway\": \"urban greenway\", \"season\": \"summer\", \"meanPRS\": 3.18, \"sd\": 1.21}, \"WG_summer\": {\"greenway\": \"wilderness greenway\", \"season\": \"summer\", \"meanPRS\": 4.72, \"sd\": 1.27}}}</script>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#edf2f4;--card:#fff;--ink:#16212a;--muted:#55636e;--accent:#1f6f8b;--line:#d2dde3;--warn:#b3261e;--sel:#d8ecf3}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:22px 16px 40px}\nh1{font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 8px}h2{font-size:1.08rem;margin:0 0 4px}p{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:16px 18px;margin-top:14px}\n.btn{appearance:none;border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 20px;font:inherit;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;background:var(--accent);color:#fff}\n.btn:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:not-allowed}\n.prog{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px}\n.prompt{font-size:.92rem;color:var(--muted);margin:6px 0 0;text-align:center}\n.scene{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:3;background:var(--bg);padding-bottom:6px}\n.scene img{max-width:100%;max-height:42vh;width:auto;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;border-radius:10px}\n@media (max-height:700px),(max-width:600px){.scene{position:static}}\n.it{padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}\n.it .st{font-weight:600;margin-bottom:6px;font-size:.96rem}\n.it .o{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(7,minmax(0,1fr));gap:4px}\n.it label{display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;text-align:center;gap:4px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:7px 4px;cursor:pointer;font-size:.84rem;line-height:1.25}\n.it label:has(input:checked){background:var(--sel);border-color:var(--accent)}\n.it label input{display:none}.it .an{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:.74rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:3px}@media (max-width:480px){.it .o{gap:3px}.it label{padding:9px 0;font-size:.86rem}}\n.it .an{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:.74rem;color:var(--muted);margin-top:3px}\n.it.miss .o,.q.miss{outline:2px solid var(--warn);outline-offset:2px;border-radius:8px}\n.q{margin-top:16px}.q:first-child{margin-top:0}\nlabel.opt{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;margin-top:6px;cursor:pointer}\ninput[type=text]{font:inherit;padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;width:100%;max-width:420px;margin-top:6px}\n.err{color:var(--warn);margin-top:8px;min-height:1.2em}\n.credit{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 16px 24px;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted)}\nlabel.opt{font-size:.95rem}\ninput[type=text]{font:inherit;padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;width:100%;max-width:420px;margin-top:6px}\n.brief{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:4px solid var(--accent);border-radius:10px;padding:12px 14px;margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--ink)}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main id=\"app\" aria-live=\"polite\"><p>Loading…</p></main>\n<footer class=\"credit\">Images: video screenshots from Wang, Liu, Zhang &amp; Wang (2025), Frontiers in Psychology 16: 1596154, Table 1 (doi:10.3389/fpsyg.2025.1596154, CC BY 4.0). Rating items: short Perceived Restorativeness Scale in the English wording printed by Negrín, Hernández-Fernaud, Hess &amp; Hernández (2017), Frontiers in Psychology 8: 1735 (doi:10.3389/fpsyg.2017.01735, CC BY 4.0).</footer>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var KEY='forest-greenway:state';\n  var ORIG=JSON.parse(document.getElementById('gw-original').textContent), IDS=ORIG.images;\n  var app=document.getElementById('app'), Q={}, files={}, st=null;\n  var BG=['gender'];\n  function esc(s){return String(s==null?'':s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;'}[c];});}\n  function err(m){var e=app.querySelector('.err');if(e)e.textContent=m||'';}\n  function ok(r){return !(r&&r.ok===false);}\n  function save(){try{localStorage.setItem(KEY,JSON.stringify(st));}catch(e){}}\n  function send(list,b,next){if(b)b.disabled=true;Promise.all(list).then(function(rs){var bad=rs.filter(function(r){return !ok(r);})[0];if(bad){if(b)b.disabled=false;return err(bad.error);}next();});}\n  function shuffle(a){a=a.slice();for(var i=a.length-1;i>0;i--){var j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1)),t=a[i];a[i]=a[j];a[j]=t;}return a;}\n  function fresh(){return {step:'intro',order:shuffle(IDS),k:0};}\n  function chs(q){return (q.choices||[]).map(function(c){return typeof c==='string'?{value:c,text:c}:c;});}\n  function field(n){var q=Q[n];\n    if(q.type==='text')return '<div class=\"q\" data-q=\"'+n+'\"><b>'+esc(q.title)+'</b>'+(q.isRequired?'':' <span style=\"color:var(--muted);font-weight:400\">(optional)</span>')+'<br><input type=\"text\" id=\"t_'+n+'\" maxlength=\"120\"></div>';\n    return '<div class=\"q\" data-q=\"'+n+'\"><b>'+esc(q.title)+'</b>'+chs(q).map(function(c){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"'+n+'\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\"> '+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div>';}\n  function intro(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Forest greenway scenes</h1><p>You will see six pictures of walking paths in urban forests, one at a time. Imagine you are walking there, and rate each picture on five short statements. It takes about 5 minutes.</p>'+\n     '<div class=\"card\"><label class=\"opt\" style=\"margin-top:0\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ok\"> '+esc(Q.consent.title)+'</label><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Start</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){if(!document.getElementById('ok').checked)return err('Consent is needed to continue.');\n      send([SPSite.answer('consent',true)],this,function(){st.step='about';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function about(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h2>About you</h2><div class=\"card\">'+BG.map(field).join('')+'<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Continue</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){var list=[];\n      for(var i=0;i<BG.length;i++){var n=BG[i],q=Q[n],v;\n        if(q.type==='text'){v=document.getElementById('t_'+n).value.trim();if(!v){if(q.isRequired){app.querySelector('[data-q='+n+']').classList.add('miss');return err('Please answer: '+q.title);}continue;}}\n        else{var x=app.querySelector('input[name='+n+']:checked');if(!x){app.querySelector('[data-q='+n+']').classList.add('miss');app.querySelector('[data-q='+n+']').scrollIntoView({block:'center'});return err('Please answer: '+q.title);}v=x.value;}\n        list.push(SPSite.answer(n,v));}\n      send(list,this,function(){st.step='scene';st.k=0;save();route();});};\n  }\n  function scene(){\n    var id=st.order[st.k],f=files[id],q=Q.prs;\n    app.innerHTML='<div class=\"prog\">Picture '+(st.k+1)+' of '+st.order.length+'</div><div class=\"scene\"><img alt=\"Walking path in an urban forest\" src=\"'+esc(f.url)+'\"></div>'+\n      '<div class=\"card\"><h2>'+esc(q.title)+'</h2>'+(q.rows||[]).map(function(r){var nm='c__'+r.value;\n      return '<div class=\"it\" data-n=\"'+nm+'\"><div class=\"st\">'+esc(r.text)+'</div><div class=\"o\">'+[1,2,3,4,5,6,7].map(function(v){return '<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"'+nm+'\" value=\"'+v+'\">'+v+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div><div class=\"an\"><span>1 '+esc(ORIG.anchors[0])+'</span><span>7 '+esc(ORIG.anchors[1])+'</span></div></div>';}).join('')+'</div>'+\n      '<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">'+(st.k<st.order.length-1?'Next picture':'Finish')+'</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){\n      var a={},miss=[];(q.rows||[]).forEach(function(r){var nm='c__'+r.value,x=app.querySelector('input[name=\"'+nm+'\"]:checked');if(x)a[r.value]=Number(x.value);else miss.push(app.querySelector('.it[data-n=\"'+nm+'\"]'));});\n      if(miss.length){miss.forEach(function(el){el.classList.add('miss');});miss[0].scrollIntoView({block:'center'});return err('Please answer every line.');}\n      send([SPSite.answer('prs',a,{key:id,shown:[f.name]})],this,function(){st.k++;if(st.k>=st.order.length)st.step='done';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function finish(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Thank you!</h1><div class=\"card\"><p id=\"fin\">Submitting…</p><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    SPSite.complete().then(function(r){if(!ok(r)){err(r.error||'Some answers are missing.');setTimeout(function(){st.step='intro';save();route();},1800);}\n      else{try{localStorage.removeItem(KEY);}catch(e){}var s=document.getElementById('fin');if(s)s.textContent='Your answers are saved.';}});\n  }\n  app.addEventListener('change',function(e){var r=e.target.closest&&(e.target.closest('.it')||e.target.closest('.q'));if(r){r.classList.remove('miss');if(!app.querySelector('.miss'))err('');}});\n  function route(){var s=st.step;window.scrollTo(0,0);if(s==='about')return about();if(s==='scene')return scene();if(s==='done')return finish();intro();}\n  SPSite.onReady(function(ctx){\n    ['consent','prs'].concat(BG).forEach(function(n){Q[n]=SPSite.getQuestion(n)||{name:n};});\n    (SPSite.getMedia('scenes')||[]).forEach(function(f){files[f.name.replace(/\\.[^.]+$/,'')]=f;});\n    var need=IDS.filter(function(k){return !files[k];});\n    if(need.length){app.innerHTML='<h1>Images missing</h1><p>Upload '+esc(need.join(', '))+' (.jpg) to the media folder \"scenes\".</p>';return;}\n    try{st=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY));}catch(e){st=null;}\n    var a=(ctx&&ctx.answers)||{};\n    if(!(st&&st.order&&st.order.length===IDS.length)||a.consent!==true)st=fresh();\n    save();route();\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
